    "cap_dependence_warning": "the dollar weighted mean SVI of the funded set is not a fixed property of this corridor or of the optimizer, it is a function of where the budget axis happens to stop. across the 80 reported budget levels between 0 and the currently configured cap of 200000 USD alone it ranges from 0.4075 to 0.7561, not monotone, it falls and then rises as the budget axis moves, an external review additionally showed that raising the cap further, to 2,000,000 USD, moves the same statistic to roughly 0.4538 against the same 0.4075 baseline, a swing of about 5.5x in effect size versus the 0.662 read at the 200,000 USD cap used elsewhere in this repository. a single number quoted at one arbitrary cap is not defensible and should not be reported or interpreted as an equity finding on its own, only the curve above, together with its range, should be quoted",
    "three_distinct_tract_value_caveat": "only 3 distinct census tracts overlap the 172 walk segments in this study area, so svi takes only that many distinct values across the whole corridor. every number in this section, the curve, its range, and the verdict below, is therefore effectively a statement about which of those few tracts happens to contain the cheapest cost effective segments at a given budget level, not a fine grained equity signal. the curve should not be read as implying more precision than a 3-value statistic can support",
