    "verdict": "the sign and size of any gap between the dollar weighted mean SVI of the funded set and the simple baseline mean depends on where the budget axis stops, see dollar_weighted_mean_svi_curve and cap_dependence_warning above. at the currently configured cap of 200000 USD the gap reads as 0.2545 (funded set above baseline), but this is one point on a curve that already ranges from 0.4075 to 0.7561 inside this repository's own solutions.json, and moves further outside that range if the cap changes, the greedy cost effectiveness objective has no SVI term anywhere in it, so any pattern here is a byproduct of which segments happen to be cost effective at a given spend level, not evidence of SVI aware behavior in either direction"
