  "unmodeled_repeat_worker_population": {
    "population_not_modeled": "stadium staff, concession and merchandise vendors, parking lot attendants and event security who walk an approach corridor repeatedly across a season rather than once as a ticketed fan does, this population is invisible to every number elsewhere in this pipeline, which is built around a single fan trip",
    "why_it_matters_for_equity": "service and gig staff at large Gulf Coast stadium events are disproportionately drawn from lower income, higher SVI neighborhoods relative to ticket buyers, this is a plausible equity concern based on general labor market patterns for stadium service work, it is not measured in this pipeline, no worker home address or wage data was fetched or is available here",
    "assumption_stated": "illustrative only, assumes a worker walks the full lot_c approach corridor (56 segments) once inbound and once outbound for every one of the 7 Houston NRG World Cup matches listed in pipeline/s7_cities.py, that match count itself is typed from general knowledge in this repository and is flagged there as unverified against FIFA's official schedule, giving 14 total one-way walks across the tournament, and further assumes every walk occurs under the same modeled kickoff-hour heat conditions used for the fan model, which ignores that a worker's actual shift start and end times, breaks, and indoor time differ from a fan's single walk to their seat",
    "one_way_trip_degmin_this_approach_measured": 55.8,
    "illustrative_cumulative_degmin_across_shifts": 780.7,
